# Brewmie Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# '/' is the marketing landing page. The web app lives at /app/: /app is normalised to /app/
# (301), and the SPA shell is served by Pages' BUILT-IN single-page fallback (index.html for
# any path with no file), which is why there is no public/404.html: adding one on 2026-10-22
# disabled that fallback and /app/ went 404. brewmie-78 is now answered by a Pages Function
# (functions/[[path]].js, routing in functions/_lib/decide.js, scope in public/_routes.json):
# it runs only for '/' and for paths that match no file, returns a real 404 for the latter and
# the landing page with 200 for '/'. It never runs for /app, /app/*, assets, fonts, translations,
# /ota or any file in public/, so the shell keeps using the built-in fallback.
# The function ships ONLY when `wrangler pages deploy dist` runs from the repo root (it reads
# ./functions; there is no --functions flag). Verify on a PREVIEW deployment first
# (BUILD_AUTOMATION.md section 4d). If '/' still answers 308 on preview, Pages applies this
# file before the function: delete the '/' line below, redeploy preview, and re-check.
# The shell keeps Vite's relative base ('./', needed by Capacitor and OTA), so under /app/ its
# relative URLs are mapped back to the real root paths below (brewmie-79: the old fallback
# served HTML for those assets).

/   /landing.html   200
/app   /app/   301
/app/assets/*   /assets/:splat   200
/app/fonts/*   /fonts/:splat   200
/app/translations/*   /translations/:splat   200
/app/manifest.json   /manifest.json   200
